@startuml sequence_post_comment
title Sequence Diagram: Post Comment

actor User as user
participant Browser as browser
participant Django as django
participant CommentPostView as view
participant CommentForm as form
participant Comment as comment
participant Article as article
participant BlogSettings as settings
participant Database as db

== User Submits Comment ==

user -> browser: Submit comment form
activate browser
browser -> django: POST /comment/article/<id>/
activate django
django -> view: CommentPostView.post()
activate view

== Form Validation ==

view -> form: CommentForm(data)
activate form
form --> view: Form is valid?
deactivate form

alt Form Valid
    view -> article: Get article by id
    activate article
    article --> view: Return article
    deactivate article

    view -> settings: Get blog settings
    activate settings
    settings --> view: Return settings
    deactivate settings

    view -> comment: Create comment instance
    activate comment
    comment -> comment: Set comment.article = article
    comment -> comment: Set comment.author = user

    alt Need Review
        comment -> comment: Set is_enable = False
    else No Review Required
        comment -> comment: Set is_enable = True
    end

    alt Has Parent Comment
        view -> comment: Set parent_comment
    end

    comment -> db: INSERT INTO comments_comment
    activate db
    db --> comment: Return success
    deactivate db
    comment --> view: Return comment object
    deactivate comment

    view -> django: HttpResponseRedirect to article page
    deactivate view
    django -> browser: Redirect response
    deactivate django
    browser -> user: Display article page with new comment
    deactivate browser
else Form Invalid
    view -> django: Return error response
    deactivate view
    django -> browser: Display error message
    deactivate django
    browser -> user: Show form validation errors
    deactivate browser
end

@enduml
